=== SIGNATURE ===
selections(arr, n, [order_matters], [repeats_allowed], [countdown_mode], [clean_inputs], [delim])

=== COMMENT ===
All combinations (default) or permutations of n items drawn from arr, ONE PER CELL as a delimited string ("1;2;3"), in a vertical list. repeats_allowed 1 lets an item be reused; countdown_mode 1 also lists every size from n down to 1; clean_inputs 1 (default) de-duplicates arr and drops blanks; delim defaults to ";".

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(arr, n_in, [order_matters], [repeats_allowed], [countdown_n], [clean_input], [delim],
 LET(n, z_num(n_in),
 IF(
  n < 1,
  NA(),
  LET(
   ci_, z_opt(1, clean_input),
   sep_, z_opt(";", delim, TRUE),
   flat_, IF(
    ci_ = 1,
    LET(r_, TOCOL(arr, 3), UNIQUE(FILTER(r_, r_ <> ""))),
    TOCOL(arr)
   ),
   m_, ROWS(flat_),
   om_, z_opt(0, order_matters),
   rep_, z_opt(0, repeats_allowed),
   cd_, z_opt(0, countdown_n),
   chars_, UNICHAR(SEQUENCE(, m_, 20001)),
   one_k_, LAMBDA(k_,
    IF(
     k_ < 1,
     NA(),
     LET(
      seq_, SEQUENCE(, k_),
      built_, REDUCE(
       "",
       seq_,
       LAMBDA(acc_, step_,
        TOCOL(
         IFS(
          IF(
           om_ = 1,
           IF(rep_ = 1, 1, ISERR(FIND(chars_, acc_))),
           IF(
            rep_ = 1,
            RIGHT(acc_) <= chars_,
            RIGHT(acc_) < chars_
           )
          ),
          acc_ & chars_
         ),
         3
        )
       )
      ),
      LET(_sel,
       MAP(built_, LAMBDA(s_, TEXTJOIN(sep_, TRUE, INDEX(flat_, UNICODE(MID(s_, seq_, 1)) - 20000)))),
       IF(ISERROR(_sel), NA(), _sel))
     )
    )
   ),
   IF(
    cd_ = 0,
    one_k_(n),
    LET(
     max_k_, IF(rep_ = 1, n, MIN(n, m_)),
     IF(
      max_k_ = 1,
      one_k_(1),
      REDUCE(
       one_k_(max_k_),
       SEQUENCE(max_k_ - 1, 1, max_k_ - 1, -1),
       LAMBDA(acc_, k_, VSTACK(acc_, one_k_(k_)))
      )
     )
    )
   )
  )
 ))
)

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Lists every way of choosing n items from arr. Each selection is ONE cell: its items joined with delim (";" by default), so selections({1;2;3}, 2) returns the three cells "1;2", "1;3", "2;3" - the form a competition answer usually wants, and easy to count, filter, split (TEXTSPLIT) or look up.

Arguments:
  arr               - the items (any shape; read row by row). With clean_inputs 1 (default) blanks are dropped and duplicates removed first.
  n                 - how many items per selection (1 or more).
  [order_matters]   - 0 (default) combinations: "1;2" and "2;1" are the same selection and only "1;2" is listed. 1 permutations: both are listed.
  [repeats_allowed] - 0 (default) an item appears at most once per selection. 1 an item may be reused ("1;1").
  [countdown_mode]  - 0 (default) only size n. 1 lists size n, then n-1, ... down to 1, stacked in one column.
  [clean_inputs]    - 1 (default) de-duplicate arr and drop blanks; 0 use arr as given.
  [delim]           - text placed between the items (default ";"; "" joins with nothing, e.g. "abc").

Order of the list: items keep the order they have in arr; selections are generated lexicographically in that order (all those starting with the first item first). Within countdown mode the larger sizes come first.

Sizes: combinations without repeats count C(m, n) and permutations P(m, n) (m = number of distinct items); with repeats m^n permutations. Excel's limits apply - a few hundred thousand selections is fine, millions is not.

Edge cases: n < 1 returns #N/A; n larger than the number of distinct items (without repeats) returns #N/A for that size (in countdown mode the impossible sizes are skipped, so countdown over 3 items with n = 5 starts at size 3). Every result cell is text, including single-item selections.

Single-value arguments (n, the flags, delim) may be given as 1x1 arrays, numbers as text, or pointed at blank cells - z_num / z_opt normalise them.

Returns:
  A vertical array of text, one selection per cell.

Example:
  selections({1;2;3}, 2)            ->  {"1;2"; "1;3"; "2;3"}
  selections({"a";"b";"c"}, 2, 1)   ->  {"a;b"; "a;c"; "b;a"; "b;c"; "c;a"; "c;b"}
  selections({"a";"b"}, 2, 0, 1)    ->  {"a;a"; "a;b"; "b;b"}
  selections({1;2;3}, 3, 0, , 1)    ->  {"1;2;3"; "1;2"; "1;3"; "2;3"; "1"; "2"; "3"}
  selections({"a";"b";"c"}, 2, , , , , "")  ->  {"ab"; "ac"; "bc"}
